#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:2
msgid "``script`` tasks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:4
msgid ""
"**Script tasks** consist of a reference to a python callable to import and "
"execute, and optionally values or expressions to pass as arguments, for "
"example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:6
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks]\n"
"fetch-assets.script = \"my_pkg.assets:fetch\"\n"
"fetch-images.script = \"my_pkg.assets:fetch(only='images', "
"log=environ['LOG_PATH'])\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:12
msgid ""
"As in the second example, it is possible to hard code literal arguments to "
"the target callable. In fact a subset of Python syntax, operators, and "
"globals can be used inline to define the arguments to the function using "
"normal Python syntax, including environ (from the os package) to access "
"environment variables that are available to the task."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:14
msgid ""
"If extra arguments are passed to task on the command line (and no CLI args "
"are declared), then they will be available within the called Python function "
"via :python:`sys.argv`. If :doc:`args <../options>` are configured for the "
"task then they will be available as Python variables."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:16
msgid ""
"If the target Python function is an async function then it will be executed "
"with :python:`asyncio.run`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:20
msgid "Available task options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:22
msgid ""
"``script`` tasks support all of the :doc:`standard task options <../"
"options>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:24
msgid "The following options are also accepted:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:26
msgid "**print_result** : ``bool`` :ref:`📖<Output the return value>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:25
msgid "bool 📖"
msgstr "bool 📖"

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:27
msgid ""
"If true then the return value of the python callable will be output to "
"stdout, unless it is ``None``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:29
msgid ""
"**ignore_fail** : ``bool`` | ``list[int]``  :ref:`📖<Ignore task failure>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:28
msgid "bool | list[int]  📖"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:30
msgid ""
"Return exit code 0 even if the task fails, or specify a list of task exit "
"codes to ignore."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:34
msgid "Update the PYTHONPATH to access scripts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:36
msgid ""
"The module containing the function for the ``script`` task to call must be "
"importable by the task subprocess running with whatever environment the "
"PoeExecutor uses (e.g. the uv or poetry managed venv)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:38
msgid ""
"This is fine if functions for poe tasks are defined alongside other source "
"in a `./src/tasks` directory for instance, but sometimes it's convenient to "
"place scripts for a project somewhere like ``./scripts/my_script.py``, which "
"will not normally be on the python path. We can still call functions from "
"the ``my_script`` module by setting the standard ``PYTHONPATH`` environment "
"variable on the task like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:40
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks.my-task]\n"
"script = \"my_script:my_function\"\n"
"env.PYTHONPATH = \"scripts\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:48
msgid "Run a ``__main__`` module as a script task"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:50
msgid ""
"A script task may reference a package instead of a specific callable, in "
"which case the package's ``__main__.py`` module will be executed as a script "
"task, or the module itself if it's not a package (the usual behavior from "
"``python -m``). This is useful for running a package or module that has been "
"designed to be run as a script."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:52
msgid ""
"For example, the following task will run the ``http.server`` module as a "
"script task, which will start a simple HTTP server. Any command line "
"arguments passed to the task will be forwarded to the script."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:54
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks.serve]\n"
"script = \"http.server\"\n"
"args = [\n"
"  { name = \"port\", options = [\"-p\"], default = \"8000\" },\n"
"  { name = \"bind\", options = [\"-b\", \"--bind\"], default = "
"\"127.0.0.1\" },\n"
"]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:63
msgid ""
"When :doc:`args <../options>` are declared on the task, the parsed values "
"(with defaults applied) are re-emitted onto the module's :python:`sys.argv`. "
"CLI tokens that aren't matched by a declared arg, and any tokens that "
"follow :sh:`--`, are forwarded to the module verbatim."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:65
msgid ""
"Like the callable form, the module form also implicitly adds :sh:"
"`<project_root>/src` to the subprocess :sh:`PYTHONPATH` so that modules "
"placed in a ``src/`` directory at the project root are importable without "
"extra configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:69
msgid "Output the return value"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:71
msgid ""
"Script tasks can be configured to output the return value of the python "
"callable using the :toml:`print_result` option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:73
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks.create-secret]\n"
"script = \"django.core.management.utils:get_random_secret_key()\"\n"
"print_result = true"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:79
msgid ""
"Given the above configuration running the following command would output "
"just the generated key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:82
msgid "poe -q create-secret"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:86
msgid ""
"Note that if the return value is None then the :toml:`print_result` option "
"has no effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:91
msgid "Calling standard library functions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:93
msgid ""
"Any python callable accessible via the python path can be referenced, "
"including the standard library. This can be useful for ensuring that tasks "
"work across platforms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:96
msgid "For example, the following task will not always work on windows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:98
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks.build]\n"
"cmd = \"mkdir -p build/assets\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:103
msgid "whereas the same behaviour can be reliably achieved like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:105
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks.build]\n"
"script = \"os:makedirs('build/assets', exist_ok=True)\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:112
msgid "Poe scripts library"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:114
msgid ""
"Poe the Poet includes the ``poethepoet.scripts`` package including the "
"following functions as convenient cross-platform implementations of common "
"task capabilities. These functions can be referenced from script tasks if "
"``poethepoet`` is available in the project virtual environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.11/site-packages/poethepoet/scripts/_rm.py:docstring
#: of poethepoet.scripts._rm.rm:1
msgid ""
"This function is intended for use in a script task to delete files and "
"directories matching any of the given patterns, as a platform agnostic "
"alternative to ``rm -rf [patterns]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.11/site-packages/poethepoet/scripts/_rm.py:docstring
#: of poethepoet.scripts._rm.rm:5
msgid "Example usage:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.11/site-packages/poethepoet/scripts/_rm.py:docstring
#: of poethepoet.scripts._rm.rm:7
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks.clean]\n"
"script = \"poethepoet.scripts:rm('.mypy_cache', '.pytest_cache', './**/"
"__pycache__')\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:0
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.11/site-packages/poethepoet/scripts/_rm.py:docstring
#: of poethepoet.scripts._rm.rm:12 poethepoet.scripts._rm.rm:13
msgid ""
"One or more paths to delete. `Glob patterns <https://docs.python.org/3/"
"library/glob.html>`_ are supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.11/site-packages/poethepoet/scripts/_rm.py:docstring
#: of poethepoet.scripts._rm.rm:15
msgid ""
"The directory relative to which patterns are evaluated. Defaults to ``.``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.11/site-packages/poethepoet/scripts/_rm.py:docstring
#: of poethepoet.scripts._rm.rm:17
msgid ""
"An integer for setting the function's verbosity. This can be set to "
"``environ.get('POE_VERBOSITY')`` to match the verbosity of the poe "
"invocation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.11/site-packages/poethepoet/scripts/_rm.py:docstring
#: of poethepoet.scripts._rm.rm:20
msgid ""
"If true then nothing will be deleted, but output to stdout will be "
"unaffected. This can be set to ``_dry_run`` to make poe delegate dry_run "
"control to the function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:121
msgid "Delegating dry-run behavior to a script"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:123
msgid ""
"Normally if the ``--dry-run`` global option is passed to the CLI then poe "
"will go through the motions of running the given task, including logging to "
"stdout, without actually running the task."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:125
msgid ""
"However it is possible to configure poe to delegate respecting this dry run "
"flag to an invoked script task, by passing it the ``_dry_run`` variable. "
"When this variable is passed as an argument to the Python function called "
"within a script task then poe will always call the task, and delegate "
"responsibility to the script for making sure that no side effects occur when "
"run in dry-run mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:129
msgid "Task arguments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:131
msgid ""
"As with other task types, script tasks support configuring named arguments "
"via the ``args`` option. Arguments are accessible in the referenced Python "
"function in three ways:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:133
msgid ""
"As **Python variables** that can be referenced directly in the function call "
"expression. Values retain their configured type — booleans are ``True``/"
"``False``, integers are ``int``, multiple args are ``list``, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:134
msgid ""
"Via **sys.argv** which is populated with the full invocation including any "
"extra arguments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:135
msgid ""
"As **keyword arguments** when the script reference doesn't include explicit "
"parentheses — in this case all declared args are passed as kwargs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:137
msgid "See :ref:`Arguments for script tasks` for more details and examples."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:141
msgid "Accessing free arguments via ``_extra_args``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:143
msgid ""
"Free arguments (arguments not matched by any named arg definition, or "
"arguments passed after :sh:`--`) are available inside script tasks as the "
"``_extra_args`` variable — a ``list[str]`` — in addition to the "
"``$POE_EXTRA_ARGS`` environment variable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/script.rst:145
msgid ""
"See the :ref:`forwarding-free-arguments-via-poe-extra-args` section of the "
"args guide for details and examples."
msgstr ""
